      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This investigation optimizes structurally engineered ionizable lipids by precisely tuning the pKa transition temperature and alkyl chain hydrophobicity within Lipid Nanoparticles (LNPs) to facilitate rapid pH-triggered membrane fusion and endosomal escape. The optimized low-cumene olefinic domains disrupt the negatively charged phospholipid bilayer electrostatics, ensuring robust cytosolic delivery of mRNA encoding tumor suppressors via the protonation-sensing switch mechanism inherent to these Delivery Vehicles. Consequently, these mechanistic refinements in Lipid Carrier architecture overcome the kinetic barriers of exosomes, significantly enhancing intracellular protein translation efficiency and genetic silencing fidelity. Ultimately, these findings provide a rigorous structural blueprint for advancing next-generation Naked Gene Therapy protocols in precision oncology applications.",
      "source": "target",
